      ],
      "title": "KPG 193: Korean Power Grid test system",
      "summary": "A 193-bus system for Korea — demand, a committed thermal fleet with cost curves, and a solved operating point. The first model here that can be run rather than only drawn.",
      "description": "The 193-bus synthetic Korean power grid (KPG 193 v2.0.0) from the AGM Center at KENTECH, by Geonho Song and Jip Kim (arXiv:2411.14756), registered here as a Sienna system. Unlike the Hub's other reference models this is a system and not a bare network: 193 buses carrying 66,135 MW of demand, 201 thermal units totalling 113 GW of capacity with quadratic cost curves and commitment state, 385 AC branches and two HVDC links. Transmission-line topology comes from OpenStreetMap via the Overpass API, the same upstream as the Great Britain and Germany models. What differs is the buses: they are clusters on the locations of KEPCO's regional offices rather than individual substations, which is what the authors mean by synthetic and why this record is filed at zonal rather than nodal spatial granularity. Impedances are per unit on a 100 MVA base, because 184 of the 385 branches join different voltage levels with no transformer ratio and so have no single base voltage to convert against. The case is one solved hour — 2025-12-31, hour 24 — and not a generic starting point: the unit commitment, dispatch and bus voltage state are an AC OPF result, which is why 101 of the 201 units are offline. The hourly demand and renewable profiles and the renewable fleet are published upstream and are not carried here, so the generators in this document are the conventional fleet only: 115 LNG, 60 coal, 26 nuclear.",
      "fidelityClass": "screening",
      "networkElementCount": 974,
      "hasTopology": true,
      "hasImpedance": true,
      "voltageClass": [
        "transmission"
      ],
      "spatialGranularity": "zonal",
      "hasField": [
        "https://catalog.opengrid.org/field/kpg-193/geometry",
        "https://catalog.opengrid.org/field/kpg-193/base-voltage",
        "https://catalog.opengrid.org/field/kpg-193/line-x",
